The 20-s sensor tags are essentially steady/noisy, and the lab Fe assay is repeated as the same hourly value (65.26%). With no silica analyzer, the most defensible estimate is a mineralogical mass balance: assume hematite-dominant iron oxide (Fe fraction a ≈ 0.6994) and a constant gangue mineralogy between feed and concentrate.

Using the linear Fe–SiO2 relation for the same ore:

\[
SiO_{2,conc}\approx 13.32\times \frac{a-0.6526}{a-0.5553}
\approx 13.32\times \frac{0.6994-0.6526}{0.6994-0.5553}
\approx 4.33\text{ wt%}
\]

<answer>4.33</answer>
